 and so  it appears to revolve slowly then time  passes and there's less and less tape  left on the reel it spins faster it  spins faster these days Reeves is trying  to move just as fast as a spinning tape  he's revisiting old franchises like the  Matrix and Bill and Ted while continuing  to push forward on more recent hits  notably there are currently two John  Wick sequels in production at the same  time he's releasing poetry showing up in  video games and spending time with the  people closest to him he said work  doesn't slow time down if anything it  speeds everything up luckily for us  Reeves still has plenty of tape left on  his reel  Keanu Reeves's career stretches right  back into the 1980s man well let's just  say he's had his fair share of ups and  downs from killer action flicks and  heartwarming dramas to tacky Thrillers  and cheap sci-fi these are the best and  worst Keanu Reeves movies  everyone knows that a dog is a man's  best friend so when a group of Russian  gangsters break into John Wick's home  kill his puppy and drive off in his car  he does what any notorious assassin  would do he makes it his mission to hunt  these men down and Destroy them but make  no mistake John Wick is more than just a  montage of mindless fight scenes the  cinematography is striking the pacing  will keep you hooked and the World  building is genuinely intriguing on top  of that Reeves's performance is a man  haunted by grief and loss is absolutely  top-notch and it doesn't exactly hurt  that he Nails the action sequences  either so far the original film has  spawned two sequels John Wick chapter 2  and John Wick chapter 3 Parabellum both  movies have earned positive receptions  from critics and audiences and the story  is even set to continue in May 2022 with  another installment John Wick chapter  four yeah I'm digging on back  and for the record every single film in  the franchise so far really has been  amazing so if you want to see Reeves as  action star best this is the place to  start  in the iffy romantic crime Thriller  Siberia Reeve stars is Lucas Hill an  American Diamond Merchant who lands  himself in trouble after traveling to  Russia to sell a rare variety of blue  diamonds to the gangster Boris volkov it  kinda seems like Lucas should have  anticipated that this transaction  wouldn't work out in his favor and sure  enough when he arrives he finds that his  contact with the diamonds has  disappeared now Lucas is desperate to  track him down before Boris comes  looking for what he's owed you'd be  forgiven for assuming that a film  involving a diamond Heist and a  forbidden romance would bring a little  more excitement to the screen than  Siberia does but sadly this movie's plot  is kind of plotting and dull but what  makes Siberia so frustrating is how  seriously this film takes itself you  can't even look at it as the kind of  movie that's so bad that it's actually  good much like an actual Trek through  Siberia the entire journey is a long  slog from beginning to end and you  wouldn't be blamed for wanting to give  up halfway through  one of the all-time classic comedies  Bill and Ted's Excellent Adventure  follows the long strange journey of high  school Slackers Bill s Preston and  Theodore Ted Logan their High School  slacker struggling to pass their  upcoming history test and even worse  Ted's father is making plans to ship him  off to military school if he can't earn  a decent grade of course doing that  would alter the course of the future as  these two are destined to save all of  humanity with their rock and roll music  so Rufus a citizen of the future travels  back to the past to help them Ace their  test as a result the heroic Duo ends up  going on a time traveling adventure  enlisting familiar historical figures to  help them pass their test it's a  fantastic premise and even though it's  one of his earliest films Reeves is  absolutely fantastic proving he's a more  than capable comedy actor of course i